A||||7||sdm1964||Polishing the rims||||7||
Z||000000||sdm1964||03-26-2000||09:37 PM||||I just got back from daytona and won second place in the Street 85 GT class. I was wondering where i can get my rims repainted and polished? I got beat out for first by one 1/2 a point. BY A GIRL!!!! good looking thought. I saw some really nice polished factory rims and forgot to get the name of the place that did them. <BR>TIA||||reg||7
Z||000001||DXR_DAD||03-26-2000||10:21 PM||||Again, congrats on the win !<P>I had my rims done, but they were done by a friend that owns a antique metal restoration shop (not a auto shop or a wheel shop) most of his stuff is brass,copper. We did a favor for a favor deal. They came out real nice, I like the stock look and the shine <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif">.<P>The pics don't do them any justice, they look much better in real life!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Check around your town for a metal fab. place like this, the price should be much less than a shop that does this type of wheel polishing all the time.<BR> <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=99075&a=723603&p=18365620&Sequence=2" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=99075&a=723603&p=18365620&Sequence=2</A> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Boxdin||03-26-2000||11:19 PM||||I took my Formula rims to the local powder coater to dip strip and coat. They looked sooo good after the dip & strip that I left them alone. I polished the outer rim with Mothers alum polish and they look perfect, with a lighter silver center, and a bright silver rim. The old black was pitted in spots and the clear was cracked. They look great now, I'm doing the same thing to my other Formula. ||||reg||6
Z||000003||Motorhead||03-27-2000||12:21 PM||||I've been thinking along those same lines.  How 'bout posting, or e-mailing me a picture of your wheels Boxdin, I'd really like to see how they came out.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Raydar||03-27-2000||12:28 PM||||Boxdin,<BR>What did they dip them in? I polished my wheels, a while back. Stripping the paint off was easily the ugliest part of the procedure.||||reg||5
Z||000005||Uaana||03-28-2000||06:12 AM||||Just a thought..<BR>anyone thought about color coding their rims<BR>to match the body color ala' grand am?||||reg||5
Z||000006||Standard||03-29-2000||02:17 AM||||never liked body colored rims.. unless your car is black or white.  i just like the machined aluminum look.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Old Lar||03-31-2000||08:55 PM||||You can get the wheels redone professionally for about $130 each.  I bought two reconditioned wheels from Kick Hill Farms.  Bob Steiger cleaned up my '87 GT wheels, but I also got points knocked off for the wheels. He cleaned up the clear coat which was really beat. <P> The Daytona judging was tough.  I got a second in the stock fastback class, which suprised me.  It was a fun show.||||reg||1
